Hmm, but the CSS convention in pages.css doesn't use `.page-` scoping. But the page-specific blocks in pages.css apply class names unique to the page (`.chips`, `.bundles`, `.thumb-*`). `.section-title` is shared. The user asked only on the products page, so I must scope. `.page-products .section-title` is correct and body has that class. Alternatively add a class to those two headings, but that changes HTML. The body class approach is clean.

