Done. I scoped the rule to the products page so the shared `.section-title` styling on other pages is untouched:

`site/css/pages.css:93`
```css
.page-products .section-title {
  font-size: 16px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
```

Verification:
- Computed styles on both headings (`All products`, `Bundles`): `font-size: 16px`, `letter-spacing: 1.28px` (= 0.08em at 16px), `text-transform: uppercase`.
- Functional tests: 16 passed.
- Visual tests: 10 unchanged, 2 changed (`products__desktop`, `products__phone`). I reviewed the diffs — the only real change is the two headings rendering as small capitals with tracking; the remaining highlighted areas are the resulting vertical shift of content (page is shorter by 20px desktop / 13px phone). All other pages are pixel-identical.

The two products baselines are pending approval, which is a human decision. To accept them: `npx testivai approve products__desktop` and `npx testivai approve products__phone` (or `/testivai approve ...`).

STATUS: DONE

